workedExamples.solution_text:
One of the ten equal parts represents $\frac{1}{10}=10\%$ of the whole.
[tikz]% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"geometry","base":[],"semantic":[{"name":"templateShade","hex":"D4E8FF","reason":"Identify the one tenth of the whole that represents 10%."}],"reference":"template ten-percent-bar-solution"}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes="1"/>}
\definecolor{templateShade}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\path[use as bounding box] (-0.6,-10.6) rectangle (50.6,0.6);
\fill[templateShade] (0,-10) rectangle (5,0);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (5,0)--(5,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (10,0)--(10,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (15,0)--(15,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (20,0)--(20,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (25,0)--(25,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (30,0)--(30,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (35,0)--(35,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (40,0)--(40,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (45,0)--(45,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (0,0) rectangle (50,-10);
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
Each part represents $500\div10=50$ litres.
